  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 253 PM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nCooler than normal conditions are expected to continue through the \nlater half of the weekend as the upper level system slowly moves \neastward. There are subtle indications that an isolated showers \nlinger into Sunday. This will depend on how quickly this shortwave \njoins a second shortwave north of the Great Lakes and is finally \nejected northeast. The upper level ridge axis begins to lean \neastward from Monday through midweek with gradual moderation to the \nairmass. Below normal temperatures rise to near seasonal normals \nthrough midweek. NBM blended guidance plots a smattering of low-end \nPoPs across the southeast section of the CWA Monday and Tuesday, \nthough the spread of potential is uncertain toward the tail end of \nthe period with the progression of the upper level trough \ndetermining the extent of precipitation potential through early week.",
